  "term": "law of frequency",
  "definition": "In historical associationist psychology, the law of frequency refers to the idea that mental connections are built by repeated joint occurrence, effectively treating frequency as a form of contiguity or habit. In the passage, it is specifically the view that perceived resemblance can be explained because similar things are often experienced together.",
